# No concrete config / display-limit value tests

Do **not** write tests whose purpose is to assert that a config key, env default, method default, display row count, or scheduled command list currently equals a specific production value.

Config and display limits exist so values can change without code changes. Locking literals in tests forces pointless test edits on every normal tweak — and calendar-window fixtures tied to “today” go flaky by day of week.

## Do not test

- `assertSame` / `assertEquals` / `assertContains` on `config('…')` or `Config::get('…')` for defaults or tunable settings
- Hardcoded production display limits / method defaults (e.g. “this week shows 3”, page size 12) as the expected count
- `schedule:list` (or `Schedule::events()`) checklists that command X / flag Y is registered
- Snapshotting arrays from config files (ignore lists, retention days, badge maps, disk names, etc.)

```php
// BAD — breaks when someone changes a default
$this->assertSame(14, config('housekeeping.log_retention_days'));
$this->assertContains('Java object is gone', config('sentry.browser.ignore_errors'));

// BAD — locks the UI row-count default; also flaky late in the week
$items = $service->itemsForThisWeek($feed, 3);
$this->assertCount(3, $items);

// BAD — schedule registry snapshot
$this->artisan('schedule:list')
    ->expectsOutputToContain('media-library:clean --delete-orphaned --force');
```

## Do test

- **Behavior under a given config/limit** — pass an explicit fixture (`Config::set(...)`, or `$limit = 2` as a local variable), then assert runtime outcome against that fixture
- **Calendar windows with frozen time** — `travelTo` / `Carbon::setTestNow` early in the window so enough in-range fixtures exist
- **Config transforms / safety rules** — e.g. staging mail must force Mailpit even if SMTP env is set
- **Infrastructure wiring that is not a tunable knob** only when the app hard-depends on it — prefer behavior tests when possible

```php
// GOOD — fixture drives behavior
Config::set('monitoring.scheduler_heartbeat_url', 'https://heartbeat.example/scheduler');
$this->artisan('monitoring:heartbeat', ['target' => 'scheduler'])->assertSuccessful();
Http::assertSent(...);

// GOOD — limit behavior, not the production default
$limit = 2;
$items = $service->itemsForThisWeek($enoughInWeekItems, $limit);
$this->assertCount($limit, $items);

// GOOD — safety rule under env
// staging APP_ENV forces mailpit host regardless of MAIL_HOST
```
